  "upload": {
    "title": "How Do You Cut a 600-Ton Stone? 🪨 #shorts",
    "description": "This slab of travertine weighs up to 600 tons, and it's cut with a wire. 🪨\n\nAt a travertine quarry, workers first drill holes through the rock. A steel cable studded with industrial diamonds runs through them and slowly saws through the stone. Then excavators push the slab away from the quarry wall until it finally falls. A section like this can weigh as much as 600 tons, heavier than about 300 cars. It's split into blocks and sold for roughly $40 to $500 a ton depending on quality, according to Business Insider.\n\nSomewhere, a kitchen countertop just got very lucky. 👇\n\nSubscribe to Top Techs for more mind-blowing tech in under a minute.",
